assertion  XSH.wctype.001
anchor     functions/wctype.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/wctype.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       wctype() returns a non-zero value for each of the twelve standard
           class names alnum, alpha, blank, cntrl, digit, graph, lower, print,
           punct, space, upper and xdigit.
test       t/001-standard-names.c

assertion  XSH.wctype.002
anchor     functions/wctype.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       wctype() returns 0 for names that name no class in the POSIX
           locale: the empty string, "no such class", "alpha " (trailing
           space) and "al pha"; none of them can be a class name, which
           has only alphanumeric characters.
test       t/002-unknown-names.c

assertion  XSH.wctype.003
anchor     functions/wctype.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/wctype.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       A handle obtained for each standard name is accepted by iswctype()
           in the locale it was obtained in: it gives non-zero for a character
           of that class and 0 for a character outside it (one of each chosen
           per class).
test       t/003-handle-usable.c

assertion  XSH.wctype.004
anchor     functions/wctype.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/wctype.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       Asking twice for the same name (with other lookups in between)
           yields handles that both give the same iswctype() answers over the
           128 characters.
test       t/004-repeatable.c

assertion  XSH.wctype.005
anchor     functions/wctype.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/wctype.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       In a UTF-8 locale the twelve standard names also give non-zero
           handles, and each handle gives non-zero from iswctype() for a
           portable character of the class that is a member in every locale
           (letters for alpha/alnum/graph/print, upper letters for upper,
           lower letters for lower, digits for digit/xdigit, space for
           space/blank).
note       Needs an installed multibyte UTF-8 locale.
test       t/005-utf8-names.c
